INFO 8622 :: Page 144 :: 1030 Am Ft Monroe Mch 5. 1865 Ft Monroe 10 am for Secy Navy Washn . Your telegram was received this morning at 15 minutes after midnight . Blowing a gale of wind at the time US steamer Ariel sailed at day - light this morning . The monitors are expected every moment from Cape fear and I shall send them up the river immediately O S. Glisson Capt Senior Officer 2.50 P. M City Pt 5th 1865 2. P. M. 5th Secy of War . Deserters from every point of the Enemys line confirm the capture of Charlottsville of Gen Sheridan they say he captured Early and nearly his entire forces consisting of eighteen hundred men . four brigades are reported as being sent to Lynchburg to get there before Gen Sheridan If possible . I think there is no doubt but Gen Sheridan will at least succeed in destroying the James river Canal U. S. Grant Lt Genl
INFO 8623 :: Page 145 :: 3.10 P. M Ft Monroe Mar. 5th 1865 Wilmington Feby 25th Via Ft Monroe 2.30 pm Mch. 5th for Q. M Gen'l Washn . Genl I am happy to inform you that we are in Wilmington . The enemy evacuated and destroyed all Gov't shops and material. I am securing all the property that will be of service to the Dept . I hope the engines and cars will be forwarded with all possible despatch please direct that two light draft propeller tug boats and two side wheel tug boats be ordered here for duty as soon as possible . This Dept is deficient in Asst Qr Masters . Please send six good efficient officers . I will send you regular reports and estimates as soon as I get the Dept organized . The Army is in good spirits . We have been crowned with success . I am Genl very Resptfully Your Obt Servt (sig) George S Dodge Col and Chief QM Dept N.C. (another) from Wilmington same date to Genl D C McCallum Washn . Wilmington is in our possession and Gen Schofield wishes the RR leading from here to Goldsboro opened up immediately . I am ready to commence work at once but have not received a single car or Locomotive yet nor any of the supplies which I have made requisition for . nothing of any importance can be done here until we get these supplies and rolling stock . If the
INFO 8624 :: Page 146 :: rolling stock has not already been shipped would it not be well to send some from City Point to this place at once . I can change the guage afterward but I must have something to work with now . I also need more men , cant you send me part of the construction force in Va until my men arrive from the west . I would like to have McAlpine with five hundred men sent here as soon as it is possible to send them WW Wright Chief Engr Govt R Roads &c 240 pm City Point Mch 6th 1865 230 pm 6th for Gen Hancock . Our own Scouts from Richmond confirm to the report of the capture of Early with most of his staff and command , those not captured have returned to Richmond with out arms . The last , the skedaddlers , Report Sheridan moving in two columns , one down the Va road towards Gordonsville and the other towards Scotts ville , about twenty thousand strong in all US Grant Lt Gen
